# ZenFlowAI Architecture Rules

## Stack
- Frontend: Next.js 15, TypeScript strict, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Framer Motion, Zustand (auth only), Apollo Client
- Backend: Express, Apollo GraphQL, Prisma, MySQL, node-cron
- Auth: JWT (15min access) + Refresh Token (7d, HTTP-only cookie)
- Real-time: GraphQL Subscriptions via graphql-ws (NOT Socket.io)

## Role Hierarchy (never change)
CUSTOMER → AGENT → SUPERVISOR → ADMIN → SUPER_ADMIN

## Security Layers (always enforced, in order)
L1 Helmet → L2 Rate Limit → L3 IP Blocklist → L4 Bot Detection →
L5 JWT Auth → L6 RBAC → L7 Data Scoping → L8 Input Validation →
L9 Spam Detection → L10 Audit Log

## Backend Rules
- Resolvers: auth check + permission check + call service. Nothing else.
- Services: business logic + Prisma. Pure when possible.
- requirePermission(ctx.role, 'resource:action') on every protected resolver
- Every write action calls audit() from security/audit.ts
- All user input goes through Zod schema validation before touching DB

## Frontend Rules
- Each route group (auth/customer/agent/supervisor/admin) is its own module
- Module structure: components/ hooks/ queries/ types.ts
- No module imports from another module's internals
- Shared UI → components/ui/
- Shared logic → lib/ (pure) or hooks/ (with side effects)
- Apollo queries live in modules/[feature]/queries/ as gql`` tagged templates
- Zustand only for auth state. Everything else = Apollo cache.

## Ticket Number Format
Generated as #ZEN-XXXX (4-digit minimum, padded)
e.g. #ZEN-0001, #ZEN-1042

## File Naming
- Components: PascalCase (TicketCard.tsx)
- Hooks: camelCase with use prefix (useTicket.ts)
- Services/utils: camelCase (ticketService.ts)
- Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE in constants.ts

## Do Not
- Never put business logic in GraphQL resolvers
- Never put DB queries outside of services/
- Never import Prisma directly in resolvers
- Never trust JWT role — always verify from DB
- Never skip audit() on sensitive mutations
- Never use `any` type
